    "created_at": "2026-01-21T10:13:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-21T10:30:54Z",
    "body": "Without the `referrerpolicy` change I think there's no observable difference. Even with `document.domain`, that doesn't change the origin returned by `ancestorOrigins` because https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin seralizes the origin's host, not the origin's domain ([demo](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14455)). There's no other way for the parent document to change its origin or its sandboxing flags after the document is created AFAIK.\r\n\r\nThere is an observable difference here though which is `[SameObject]` removal and returning a new `DOMTokenList` every time (which matches Chromium and Gecko but not WebKit). This is tested in https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-ancestor-origins-inactive-document.sub.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned and https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/56635",
