    "created_at": "2026-01-21T13:13:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-21T13:13:40Z",
    "body": "> There's no other way for the parent document to change its origin or its sandboxing flags after the document is created AFAIK.\r\n\r\nRight, well technically it changes its origin by virtue of changing its origin's domain with `document.domain`, but this doesn't impact same origin checks, only [same origin-domain](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#same-origin-domain) checks I guess. Does that match your understanding?\r\n\r\nEven with https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11560, there should be no observable change due to `document.domain`, because https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11560 only ever refers to \"same origin\" checks, never \"same origin-domain\" checks. Is this right?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
